<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 2.346 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    363 days   23.25 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   21.98 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   20.95 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     42 days   19.89 pct</p>
<p>    400 million     19 days   19.50 pct</p>
<p>    700 million     13 days   19.12 pct</p>
<p>    296 million	3 days   18.49 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
